    `<section class="card"><div class="card-header"><div><h2>Configuration comparison</h2><p class="card-intro">${state.candidates.length} candidates · fixed concurrency sweep 1–128 · all memory values per device, in GiB</p></div><button class="button small" data-action="show-all">${state.showAll?'Show shortlist':'Show all candidates'}</button></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Hardware / evidence</th><th>TP × replicas</th><th>Concurrency</th><th>Memory / budget</th><th>TTFT service</th><th>TPOT service</th><th>Capacity</th><th>Total / hour</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows.map(r=>`<tr class="clickable ${r.id===c?.id?'selected':''}" tabindex="0" role="button" data-action="select-candidate" data-id="${esc(r.id)}" aria-label="Select ${esc(r.id)}"><td><strong>${esc(hw(r.hardware_id).name)}</strong><span class="secondary">${r.evidence} ${r.run_ids.length?'· '+r.run_ids.length+' runs':''}</span></td><td>${r.tp} × ${r.replicas||'—'}<span class="secondary">${r.device_count||'—'} total devices/nodes</span></td><td>${r.concurrency}<span class="secondary">per replica</span></td><td>${fmt(r.memory.total/2**30||null)} / ${fmt(r.memory.budget/2**30||null)}</td><td>${fmt(r.ttft_service_s*1000||null)} ms${r.measured_ttft_p95_s!=null?`<span class="secondary">Measured p95: ${fmt(r.measured_ttft_p95_s*1000)} ms</span>`:''}</td><td>${fmt(r.tpot_service_s*1000||null)} ms${r.measured_tpot_s!=null?`<span class="secondary">Measured ${w.tpot_percentile}: ${fmt(r.measured_tpot_s*1000)} ms</span>`:''}</td><td>${fmt(r.total_request_capacity)} req/s<span class="secondary">${fmt(r.output_capacity_tps,0)} output tok/s</span></td><td><strong>${money(r.hourly_usd)}</strong></td><td>${badge(r.feasible?'Feasible':'Excluded',r.feasible?'ok':'danger')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="chart-note">Feasible means analytically screened, unless explicitly benchmark validated. Select a row to inspect its assumptions and failure reasons.</p></section>`+
    (c ? `<div class="split"><section class="card"><div class="card-header"><div><h2>TPOT vs. concurrency</h2><p class="card-intro">Service estimates and mean fits; measured percentile points shown when available.</p></div>${badge(c.evidence)}</div><div id="tpot-chart" class="chart"></div><p class="chart-note">The dashed target is a percentile SLO. Lines do not prove tail compliance. Diamonds are real imported measurements, with workload context in hover text.</p></section><section class="card"><div class="card-header"><div><h2>Selected configuration</h2><p class="card-intro">${esc(h.name)} · TP${c.tp} · ${c.concurrency} active sequences / replica</p></div>${badge(c.feasible?'Feasible':'Excluded',c.feasible?'ok':'danger')}</div><div id="memory-chart" class="mini-chart"></div>${c.memory.total?`<div class="stat-detail"><span>Physical memory / device</span><b>${fmt(c.memory.physical/1e9)} GB / ${fmt(c.memory.physical/2**30)} GiB</b></div>`:''}<div class="stat-detail"><span>Sustainable capacity / replica</span><b>${fmt(c.request_capacity_per_replica)} req/s</b></div><div class="stat-detail"><span>Operating period · ${fmt(w.operating_hours,0)} h</span><b>${money(c.period_usd)}</b></div><div class="stat-detail"><span>Cost / 1M total tokens</span><b>${money(c.cost_per_million_total,3)}</b></div><p class="chart-note">${esc(c.validation)}<br>${esc(c.reasons.join(' · '))}</p></section></div>` : '')+
    detail('Selected assumptions, formulas & evidence coverage',`<p>Weight bytes = parameters × effective storage bytes × (1 + format overhead) ÷ TP. KV bytes/token = 2 × layers × KV heads × head dimension × KV element bytes. Max request residency is rounded to 16-token blocks.</p><p>Decode step = max(compute time, weight + KV memory traffic time) + communication. Sustainable throughput is limited by combined prefill/decode demand and active-sequence occupancy. Replica count covers peak × burst × headroom.</p><p>Costs use all allocated devices. Per-million denominators use the requested workload, including idle headroom in the cost numerator. Decimal GB = 10⁹ bytes; GiB = 2³⁰ bytes.</p><pre class="code-light">${esc(json(c?.coverage || {}))}</pre><pre class="code-light">${esc(json(c?.memory || {}))}</pre>`)+
    detail('Explore separate prefill & decode pools',`<p>Supply a real transfer/router stack and network assumptions to compare phase-pool costs. This is an exploratory estimate and does not automatically replace the recommendation.</p><form id="disagg-form"><div class="form-grid cols-3">${select('prefill_hardware_id','Prefill hardware',state.hardware.map(h=>[h.id,h.name]),state.hardware[0].id)}${field('network_gbps','Shared network capacity',100,'Gb/s','','min="0.1"')}${field('network_efficiency','Network efficiency',0.7,'','','min="0.01" max="1"')}${field('routing_ms','Routing overhead',1,'ms','','min="0"')}${field('router_hourly_usd','Router + network cost',0,'$/h','','min="0"')}${textField('transfer_stack','Router / KV-transfer stack','','Name and version of actual supported components','required placeholder="Router + connector versions"')}</div><div class="form-foot"><p>Selected configuration supplies the decode hardware, TP, and concurrency.</p><button class="button" type="submit" ${c?.feasible?'':'disabled'}>Compare phase pools</button></div></form><div id="disagg-result"></div>`)+
    next(3,'Validate with benchmarks','Next: import observed results or connect your existing service.');
