    detail('How measurement matching & calibration work',`<p>Measurements match model commit, hardware/topology, engine/version, serving and KV precision, TP, scheduler limits, cache behavior, and workload. Qualified matching runs take precedence over heuristic estimates. Replica scaling remains unvalidated until the planned deployment is measured at the requested load.</p><p>Empirical corrections require at least three qualifying single-replica runs. Coverage, in-sample residuals, and extrapolation are shown with the selected candidate. Aggregate metrics do not uniquely identify MFU/MBU. No statistical confidence interval is claimed.</p><p>The minimum evidence floor is 200 samples, 30 seconds, 5 seconds of warmup, open-loop traffic, known arrival rate, and zero errors/timeouts. This floor is a screening rule, not a guarantee of statistical power.</p>`)+
    next(4,'Prepare exports','Next: version-scoped serving commands, a sizing report, and optional Kubernetes manifests.');
